stem:
A stylesheet contains:
body { background-color: #FFFFFF; font-family: Georgia, serif; }
.note { color: #8B0000; font-weight: bold; }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 90%; }
td { border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 6px; }

The head of a web page contains:
<link rel="stylesheet" href="main.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="summer.css">
main.css contains: p { color: #000000; font-size: 11pt; }
summer.css contains: p { color: #FF4500; }
One paragraph is written as <p style="font-size: 14pt;">Summer sale now on.</p>

parts.text:
A student has inserted a photograph into a two-column report. The teacher notes these problems:
• the photograph looks squashed;
• it overlaps the right margin by 1 cm;
• the text stops above the photograph and starts again below it, leaving large empty spaces at the sides;
• the top of the photograph covers part of the header.
For each problem, describe how the student should correct it.
